{"id": "EUVD-2026-91482", "enisaUuid": "79b3d935-60e2-308f-aabc-df5385938a70", "description": "YesWiki before 4.6.7 contains an unrestricted file upload vulnerability that allows authenticated admins to write remote files into the web-accessible files/ directory via Bazar CSV import preview. Attackers can import a CSV whose file or image field references a remote .php URL, which is saved without extension checks and executed as server-side code.", "datePublished": "2026-10-02T11:38:36", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-02T13:43:17", "baseScore": 8.6, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:H/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/YesWiki/yeswiki/security/advisories/GHSA-v3gq-c7c6-mxw3", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/yeswiki-before-4.6.7-unrestricted-file-upload-via-bazar-csv-import"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-104471", "GHSA-g4m2-8g7g-xw8c"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.37, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "b8589dde-6bb8-3c6b-a330-e67428958f43", "product": {"name": "yeswiki", "vendor": {"name": "YesWiki"}}, "product_version": "0 <4.6.7"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "90a7023e-177c-3168-9f69-5d84c6594ec7", "vendor": {"name": "YesWiki"}}], "isExploited": false}